* The glass tube from the domed lab's dock to the gene lab, walked (openc2e
* Creatures 2 project, our own script). Run by openc2e after the world
* loads (Additions folder); safe to repeat. ROOM takes all of a room's data,
* so each room's own values are passed back.
*
* The tube carried a car (the transit pod, 3 6 3) between a dock bay by the
* dome and a ledge at the gene lab's west wall. Creatures crowded the bay,
* starving, pacing at its east wall (NOTES: "The dome's tube-car crowd").
* The owner chose (2026-11-19) to take the car away and let creatures walk
* through the tube, which now slopes down from the dock to the gene lab's
* floor (its new art: tube-walk pictures, placed below). The walking line
* is the owner's: the dock's floor (y 1544) to x 4735, down over the dock's
* collar to (4801, 1569), straight down to the lab's floor (1798) at x 6023.
*
* 1. The car, its watcher and both of its callers, gone (transit.cos no
*    longer makes them; the car and the dome's dock button are the world
*    file's, made again at each load).
enum 3 6 3 kill targ next
enum 2 1 143 kill targ next
enum 2 2 219 kill targ next
enum 2 2 22 kill targ next
*
* 2. The cage lift by the huts (3 2 2, cage at x 5116 after treelift.cos)
*    no longer stops at the old deck (y 1615), where the tube now runs: the
*    deck is scaffolding holding the lift's pulley (owner, 2026-11-19). RSTP
*    (openc2e's) takes the stop and its caller away. A cage left up there
*    by the world file or a save is set on the walkway's stop (its bottom
*    at 1858), riders and all (a call would not move it: the lift only
*    answers when free, its OV00 0).
enum 3 2 2
  doif posl gt 5090 and posl lt 5140
    rstp targ 1615
    doif posb lt 1700 setv var1 1858 subv var1 hght mvto posl var1 setv ov00 0 setv vely 0 endi
  endi
next
*
